  "limits": [
    "Only the moneyline, the point spread and the game total are analyzed, each at its most-quoted number. Alternate numbers, team totals, half and quarter markets and player props are not.",
    "Every quote is the newest one captured before this packet was built, with its capture time, from the books named; nothing was captured after the packet was built or after the start.",
    "Form, rest, travel and head to head cover only the games in the data store (it begins with the 2021 season). A window holds fewer games than it names early in a season, and each figure states how many it rests on.",
    "Weather forecasts, depth charts, snap counts, play-by-play detail, officials, coaching and scheme changes and news after the weekly injury report are not in the data.",
    "The starting quarterback is the one the schedule lists, a projection until the game is played. The injury report is the weekly team report; a player's importance is not measured.",
    "A neutral-site game has a nominal home team; its differentials still read home minus away."
  ],
  "how_to_read": [
    "In sections.matchup.values.differentials a difference is home minus away, so a positive one means the home team has the larger number. head_to_head is written from the home team's side.",
    "A form window says how many games it rests on (games). last_3 and last_5 are the team's most recent finished games; season_to_date is this season only. yards_per_play is net yards per play and turnover_margin is takeaways minus giveaways per game; each states the games it rests on.",
    "A spread selection carries its own signed number: \"KC -3.5\" lays 3.5 points and \"LAC +3.5\" gets 3.5. The two selections of the spread are the two sides of one number. fair_probability is the market's probability with the bookmaker's margin divided out, averaged over the books that quoted both sides.",
    "first_captured fields give where the market stood the first time it was captured, which is not necessarily the opening line.",
    "A qb listed_for_this_game with projected true is the schedule's projection at listed_as_of_utc, not a confirmed starter. The injury report is the weekly team report as stored.",
    "figure_units says what each form figure measures. sections.reference.values holds scoring facts, not statistics."
  ]
